Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1; see LICENSE in this
directory.

The browser build embeds them because a browser has no system fonts. Native
builds include them as a final sans-serif fallback after installed fonts,
including in headless Python environments. The browser's font database also
lists these Arial-compatible faces under the family name Arial. Native builds
retain the system's generic sans-serif preference. The font files themselves
are not changed.
